What is Space Robotics?
Space robotics encompasses advanced robotic systems specifically engineered for extraterrestrial operations, spanning a broad spectrum of technologies including planetary rovers, orbital manipulators, servicing arms, and autonomous assemblers. These sophisticated systems are designed to perform critical functions such as surface exploration, satellite maintenance, in-orbit construction, and sample collection-all while operating reliably in the extreme conditions of vacuum, intense radiation, and microgravity. Key categories within the space robotics landscape include wheeled rovers, robotic arms, docking systems, and emerging humanoid robots adapted for space environments.
